---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import LegalIdentity from '../../components/LegalIdentity.astro';
import { route } from '../../i18n/routes';
import { breadcrumbSchema } from '../../lib/seo';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, LEGAL } from '../../data/site-config';
const lang = 'en';
---
<PageLayout title="Privacy Policy, SingaporeSalary.com: What We Collect" description="Privacy policy of SingaporeSalary.com under the PDPA: CPF and tax inputs stay in your browser, no cookies, no visitor records, a cookieless stability check." lang={lang} noindex={true} jsonLd={[breadcrumbSchema([{ name: 'Home', path: route('home', lang) }, { name: 'Privacy', path: route('privacy', lang) }])]} breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Privacy' }]}>
  <header class="mb-6"><h1 class="text-3xl font-bold text-navy-900 md:text-4xl">Privacy policy</h1></header>
  <div class="prose prose-slate max-w-none">
    <h2>Controller</h2>
    <LegalIdentity lang="en" />
    <h2>Salary, age and residency inputs</h2>
    <p>Working out CPF and income tax needs your monthly wage, bonus, age, residency status and reliefs. That arithmetic is done by JavaScript inside your browser tab: none of those values is transmitted to Radif Partners or to a third party, kept on a server or tied to your identity. The site has no sign-up, mailing list or form that gathers personal data. After you change a field, the address bar carries your inputs, so anyone you send that link to can see them, and nobody else.</p>
    <h2>Server logs</h2>
    <p>Pages are delivered by {LEGAL.hosting.name}, which, like every web host, logs each request (IP address, page, time, browser) to serve the site and fend off abuse. We do not go through those logs to work out who visits.</p>
    <h2>No cookies and no visitor profile</h2>
    <p>The site sets no cookie and writes nothing to your device’s storage. Radif Partners does not record personal data about its visitors and does not measure its audience.</p>
    <h2>Stability monitoring with Microsoft Clarity</h2>
    <p>The one outside script is Microsoft Clarity, loaded in cookieless mode: the page refuses storage on its behalf before the script arrives, so no <code>_clck</code>, <code>_clsk</code>, <code>MUID</code> or <code>CLID</code> cookie is created, each page view carries a separate identifier and visits stay unlinked. It tells us about JavaScript errors, slow pages, unresponsive clicks and scrolling, plus device and browser type. Page content and field entries are masked in the browser, though the values carried by a shared link are part of the address it notes. The service is run by Microsoft Ireland Operations Limited, One Microsoft Place, South County Business Park, Leopardstown, Dublin 18, Ireland; recordings are deleted after 30 days and aggregates after 13 months. Our purpose is limited to keeping the calculators reliable, a legitimate interest (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR) and a purpose a reasonable person would consider appropriate under the PDPA. Microsoft may handle this data outside Singapore, the United States included, as its <a href="https://privacy.microsoft.com/privacystatement" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">privacy statement</a> explains. To object, block clarity.ms or write to us; every calculator keeps working. The <a href={route('cookies', lang)}>cookies page</a> gives the details. No advertising script runs on the site.</p>
    <h2>PDPA and GDPR rights</h2>
    <p>Under Singapore’s Personal Data Protection Act 2012, and under the GDPR because Radif Partners is based in France, you may ask what personal data we hold about you, have it corrected or object to its use. Calculator inputs never reach us, so in practice there is nothing to hand over. Requests go to <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>; complaints can be lodged with Singapore’s Personal Data Protection Commission or with France’s {LEGAL.supervisoryAuthority}.</p>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
